cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Covert Channel Studio
message: >-
  If you use this educational lab in teaching or research, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: systemslibrarian (Covert Channel Studio contributors)
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/systemslibrarian/crypto-lab-covert-channel-studio
url: >-
  https://systemslibrarian.github.io/crypto-lab-covert-channel-studio/
abstract: >-
  An educational, fully-simulated Crypto-Lab exhibit on covert channels: hidden
  communication in protocols, timing, and media. It teaches storage vs. timing
  channels; DNS, ICMP, IP-field, ordering, HTTP-header, protocol-hopping,
  air-gap optical, shared-cache and steganographic carriers; the
  capacity/reliability/observability trade-off; and how defenders both detect
  covert channels (named, cited statistical methods, a blind detection
  challenge, a detector validation lab, and a learned detector measured for
  overfitting and distribution shift) and disrupt them (an active-warden
  normalizer lab). It runs entirely client-side and generates no real network
  traffic.
keywords:
  - covert channels
  - security education
  - steganography
  - timing channel
  - dns tunneling
  - steganalysis
  - detection
  - crypto-lab
license: MIT
